     "problem_md": "Gail uses digital devices for work.\n\nA CD drive is a type of optical storage device.\n\n(i) Give **two other **types of optical storage device.\n\n[2]\n\n(ii) One disadvantage of optical media is that it has a lower storage capacity than solid state media.\n\nExplain **two other** disadvantages of using optical media rather than solid state media.\n\n[4]",
     "solution_md": "> **[mark-scheme]**\n> (i)\n> \n> - DVD (drive)\n> - Blu-ray (drive)\n> \n> (ii)\n> \n> Two explanations, each to include **two** linked points such as:\n> \n> - Less robust / don’t last as long (1) because the disks are fragile / can scratch/snap easily (1)\n> - Slower access time (1) because solid state uses electrical charges / optical disk drives are mechanical (1)",
     "spec_point_codes": [
      "1.5.3"
     ]
    }
